      {
        "narration": "These stairs climb straight into a ceiling and stop. Down the hall, a door opens onto a two-storey drop.",
        "visual_query": "victorian mansion interior staircase wood",
        "visual_fallback": "victorian staircase"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The house is in San Jose, California. Sarah Winchester, widow of the rifle fortune, designed it herself and kept crews working.",
        "visual_query": "sprawling victorian mansion california exterior",
        "visual_fallback": "victorian mansion"
      },
      {
        "narration": "By her death in 1922 it held 160 rooms, two thousand doors and 47 separate staircases. So what was she building?",
        "visual_query": "ornate wooden door frame interior",
        "visual_fallback": "ornate door"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 1906 the San Francisco earthquake wrecked large parts of it. She had the rubble cleared and simply left the rest.",
        "visual_query": "earthquake damaged victorian house wreckage",
        "visual_fallback": "damaged house"
      },
      {
        "narration": "That is where the stairs to nowhere came from. Not ghosts. Historians say she paused for months, and mostly managed her estate.",
